usage: verify_robocasa_rgbd_pose.py [-h] --episode-dir EPISODE_DIR --report
                                    REPORT [--replay] [--raw-root RAW_ROOT]
                                    [--flat-root FLAT_ROOT]
                                    [--source-dataset SOURCE_DATASET]
                                    [--state-index-policy {frame_index}]
                                    [--frames FRAMES]
                                    [--geometry-atol-m GEOMETRY_ATOL_M]
                                    [--min-ray-samples MIN_RAY_SAMPLES]
                                    [--rgb-mae-max RGB_MAE_MAX]
                                    [--owner-visual-review-ref OWNER_VISUAL_REVIEW_REF]

Validate a committed RGB-D/Pose episode; optionally replay it on the server.
Offline cache integrity is not physical geometry acceptance. --replay
additionally checks original RGB, state restoration, per-frame camera
matrices, fresh depth and independent, renderer-filtered mj_ray geometry. No
RGB/depth images are exported. Under the Owner's spatial-v2 policy, re-
rendered RGB photometry is diagnostic. Automatic spatial checks do not attest
to a human RGB/Depth visual inspection.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --episode-dir EPISODE_DIR
  --report REPORT       new text-only JSON outside the immutable episode
  --replay
  --raw-root RAW_ROOT
  --flat-root FLAT_ROOT
  --source-dataset SOURCE_DATASET
  --state-index-policy {frame_index}
  --frames FRAMES       subset of committed frame indices; default all
                        committed frames
  --geometry-atol-m GEOMETRY_ATOL_M
  --min-ray-samples MIN_RAY_SAMPLES
  --rgb-mae-max RGB_MAE_MAX
                        photometric diagnostic threshold only; does not gate
                        spatial checks
  --owner-visual-review-ref OWNER_VISUAL_REVIEW_REF
                        external review provenance only; never automatically
                        asserts visual PASS
